          equipment: 'Double-nine domino set and flat surface.',
          dealing: 'Each player receives 8 tiles (for 4 players) or 10 tiles (for 2-3 players). The rest form the boneyard.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to play all tiles (Domino!) or have the lowest pip-count when the game is blocked. 100 points wins.',
          gameplay: "1. **Starting**: The player with the highest double leads. This double is the 'Spinner'. 2. **Individual Arms**: Each player has an 'arm' extending from the spinner. You can normally only play on your own arm. 3. **Opening an Arm**: If you cannot play a tile, you must 'Open' your arm (often marked with a coin). 4. **Public Access**: Any player can play on an 'Open' arm. The owner of the arm 'Closes' it as soon as they are able to make a play on it again. 5. **Doubles**: Doubles are played sideways and do not branch (traditional Cuban style).",
          keyRules: [
            'Highest double leads and becomes the Spinner.',
            'Each player has their own arm extending from the spinner.',
            'Can normally only play on your own arm.',
            "If cannot play, must 'Open' your armâ€”others can then play on it.",
            "Owner 'Closes' arm when they play on it again.",
            "Winner scores total pips in opponents' hands.",
            'First to 100 points wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Keep your high-pip tiles for your own arm early in the game. If you have to open your arm, you are inviting others to dump their 9s and 8s on you, making it harder for you to win the round.',
          intermediate: "Offensive Passing: Sometimes, even if you have a play, it is better to 'Pass' and open your arm if you know your opponent is holding a tile that can only be played on YOUR arm. This traps them into helping you extend your train.",
          advanced: "Boneyard Management: In Longana, the boneyard is a resource. If you have only one tile left and it's a double, you might draw from the boneyard intentionally to find a 'blocking' tile to prevent an opponent from going out before you.",
          tips: [
            "The 0-0 (Double Blank) is the 'Lurker'. It carries 0 points but can block an entire arm if no one else has a blank. Play it early if your arm is open.",
            "Watch the 'Open' arms carefully. If someone opens an arm that matches a tile you have two of, play one there immediately to clear your hand.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
